{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Abraham returned to his place.</b> To Hebron. And this vision was in the place where Abraham went to send off the angels, and from there he looked out toward Sodom — even though it is written, \"And Abraham rose early in the morning and looked out toward Sodom\" (Genesis 19:27–28), it was after the sun had gone forth, for Sodom was not overturned at night, for so Scripture testified."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:02.219373994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}